WEBVTT


00:01:37.611 --> 00:01:40.321
It's 8:00 a.m. and a glorious 74


00:01:40.488 --> 00:01:42.073
here in downtown Dallas.


00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.701
Let's kick things off with the our own
hometown sweetheart Beth Boothby.


00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:50.373
♪ I know where I'm going ♪


00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:55.337
♪ I know who goes with me ♪


00:01:55.504 --> 00:01:59.299
♪ I know who I love ♪


00:02:00.592 --> 00:02:04.970
♪ My dear knows who I'll marry ♪


00:02:05.137 --> 00:02:09.517
♪ I have stockings of silk ♪


00:02:09.683 --> 00:02:13.853
♪ Shoes of bright green leather ♪


00:02:14.021 --> 00:02:18.943
♪ Combs to buckle my hair ♪


00:02:19.109 --> 00:02:23.906
♪ And a ring for every finger ♪


00:02:25.032 --> 00:02:28.576
♪ Featherbeds are soft ♪


00:02:28.743 --> 00:02:33.081
♪ Painted rooms are bonny ♪


00:02:33.248 --> 00:02:38.043
♪ But I would give them all ♪


00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:40.088
♪ For my handsome ♪


00:02:40.255 --> 00:02:43.590
♪ Winsome Johnny ♪


00:02:43.757 --> 00:02:47.720
♪ Some say he is poor ♪


00:02:47.887 --> 00:02:53.559
♪ I say he is bonny... ♪


00:02:53.725 --> 00:02:55.770
I'm so glad
you're going with me.


00:02:55.937 --> 00:02:58.105
I couldn't let you loose among
all them heathens, honey,


00:02:58.272 --> 00:02:59.314
not on your lonesome.


00:02:59.481 --> 00:03:03.402
♪ Handsome, winsome Johnny ♪


00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:06.822
♪ I know where I'm going. ♪


00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.456
Hi, Beth. Autograph?


00:03:21.253 --> 00:03:25.047
♪ He hath filled the hungry
with good things ♪


00:03:25.214 --> 00:03:29.802
♪ And the rich he hath sent
empty away ♪


00:03:29.969 --> 00:03:33.722
♪ He hath helped
His servant Israel ♪


00:03:33.888 --> 00:03:38.853
♪ In remembrance of his mercy ♪


00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:42.941
♪ Spoke to our fathers,
to Abraham ♪


00:03:43.108 --> 00:03:45.901
♪ And to his seed ♪


00:03:46.068 --> 00:03:49.446
♪ Forever. ♪


00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.497
We are gathered here today


00:03:59.664 --> 00:04:02.584
to say Godspeed
to Beth and Steve...


00:04:02.751 --> 00:04:04.878
two of our young redeemers


00:04:05.045 --> 00:04:08.507
who are going to give two years
of their young lives to God


00:04:08.674 --> 00:04:10.550
and to bringing His message


00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.511
to the lost people of Scotland.


00:04:19.184 --> 00:04:21.518
Seemingly,
there are people there


00:04:21.685 --> 00:04:23.563
that have forgotten the Lord.


00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.940
Many, I hear, don't even
believe in angels.


00:04:27.107 --> 00:04:30.026
- Don't even believe


00:04:30.193 --> 00:04:32.656
in angels, folks.


00:04:34.324 --> 00:04:37.493
Beth, I want you to know


00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.829
that we are all
real proud of you.


00:04:40.996 --> 00:04:43.248
But you are going out there


00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:45.667
to do some service to God.


00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:48.420
And, Steve,


00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:51.964
you take real good care of this
lovely little lady, do you hear?


00:04:52.131 --> 00:04:53.216
Yes, sir.


00:04:55.802 --> 00:04:58.263
May God bless you both


00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.682
and bring you back safe,


00:05:00.848 --> 00:05:04.144
successful and pure to us here.


00:05:04.311 --> 00:05:07.355
And we will give you
the wedding of the year.


00:05:07.522 --> 00:05:09.899
And that's a promise. Amen.


00:06:20.176 --> 00:06:22.595
I'm up to my oysters


00:06:22.762 --> 00:06:25.264
in shite!


00:06:25.431 --> 00:06:27.516
Beth. Beth.


00:06:27.683 --> 00:06:30.059
<i>- You look gorgeous.
-  Give them some space.</i>


00:06:31.186 --> 00:06:34.105
Over here, Beth.
Over here.


00:06:41.821 --> 00:06:44.574
Just one more, Beth.


00:06:45.617 --> 00:06:47.494
Thank you, darling.


00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:50.455
Delia, welcome indeed.


00:06:50.622 --> 00:06:53.999
As you can see, your young guests
are already here.


00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:57.253
This is Beth Boothby.


00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.296
She and her friend
are looking forward


00:06:59.463 --> 00:07:01.632
to preaching door to door.


00:07:01.799 --> 00:07:03.801
God bless them.


00:07:03.966 --> 00:07:07.304
Beth, this is
Sir Lachlan Morrison...


00:07:07.471 --> 00:07:08.472
Pleasure.


00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:10.556
...the patron for our concert
here today.


00:07:10.723 --> 00:07:13.561
We're just so grateful
to you, sir,


00:07:13.728 --> 00:07:15.687
and lady?


00:07:15.854 --> 00:07:17.731
Oh, call us Lachlan and Delia.


00:07:17.898 --> 00:07:19.774
We don't stand
on ceremony here.


00:07:19.941 --> 00:07:21.693
And who is this?


00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:24.488
I guess you could call Steve
my fiancé.


00:07:26.322 --> 00:07:29.535
Nice to meet you, sir, ma'am.


00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.494
See our silver rings?


00:07:31.661 --> 00:07:33.955
- Oh, the same rings?
- How charming.


00:07:34.121 --> 00:07:35.831
To show that you're engaged?


00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:38.168
As a sign
of our chastity, ma'am.


00:07:39.461 --> 00:07:42.004
Beautiful. Thank you.


00:07:43.673 --> 00:07:46.384
Well, I guess it don't appeal
too much to some young folks here,


00:07:46.551 --> 00:07:48.761
but thanks to your invite,
me and Beth...


00:07:48.928 --> 00:07:50.679
we've come over here
to try and change that.


00:07:50.846 --> 00:07:52.389
- Right, baby?
- Yeah.


00:07:52.556 --> 00:07:55.101
Beth, I think
they're ready for you.


00:07:55.268 --> 00:07:57.143
Excuse me.


00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.479
Beth, Beth.


00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.241
Great.


00:08:11.408 --> 00:08:13.910
- Thank you. Bye.
- Come on, out. Out.


00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.460
They're both perfect.


00:08:23.627 --> 00:08:26.089
I was afraid we'd have to look
further afield this year.


00:08:26.255 --> 00:08:30.009
What a little star,
especially if she can sing.


00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:32.386
And rather beautiful, too.


00:08:32.553 --> 00:08:35.348
In a corn-fed, apple-cheeks
sort of way.


00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.057
A perfect mate
for a cowboy, then.


00:08:37.224 --> 00:08:38.934
Absolutely.


00:08:39.101 --> 00:08:41.437
I bet she smells of the dairy,


00:08:41.604 --> 00:08:43.856
a musky bush, milky tits


00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:48.276
and just a hint of warm
cow shit behind the ears.


00:08:48.443 --> 00:08:50.321
So you approve of her, then?


00:08:50.487 --> 00:08:52.363
Oh, and that poor Steve,


00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.407
wearing that ridiculous
silver ring


00:08:54.574 --> 00:08:56.743
and waiting
till his wedding day.


00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.414
It really is another world
over there in America, isn't it?


00:09:02.707 --> 00:09:04.751
Oh, look, they're fixing up
the mic for her.


00:09:04.918 --> 00:09:08.880
None of these pop people
can really sing.


00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:24.771
♪ I know that my Redeemer lives ♪


00:09:24.938 --> 00:09:27.607
♪ What joy the blessed... ♪


00:09:27.774 --> 00:09:30.193
I need to have a word
with that cowboy.


00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.278
Why not?


00:09:32.445 --> 00:09:35.489
♪ He lives, He lives ♪


00:09:35.656 --> 00:09:39.451
♪ That once was dead ♪


00:09:39.618 --> 00:09:41.286
♪ He lives... ♪


00:09:41.453 --> 00:09:43.663
You must be very proud.


00:09:43.829 --> 00:09:45.289
Oh, I sure am.


00:09:45.456 --> 00:09:48.001
For me, that voice of hers
is always just awesome.


00:09:48.168 --> 00:09:50.628
Papa says
she sounds like an angel.


00:09:50.795 --> 00:09:53.714
Oh, of course.
That's what she reminds me of...


00:09:53.881 --> 00:09:56.218
an angel.


00:09:56.385 --> 00:09:58.261
Do you believe in angels?


00:09:58.428 --> 00:10:00.888
Doesn't everyone?


00:10:04.558 --> 00:10:07.937
Hats in church...
it's one of our local to-dos.


00:10:08.104 --> 00:10:10.648
It makes you look even more...


00:10:10.815 --> 00:10:13.985
well, now, what would
the Americans say?


00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.027
...cute without it.


00:10:16.194 --> 00:10:20.324
♪ In time of need ♪


00:10:20.491 --> 00:10:24.161
♪ He lives, my Savior ♪


00:10:24.328 --> 00:10:27.832
♪ Still the same ♪


00:10:27.999 --> 00:10:31.126
♪ What joyful bliss ♪


00:10:31.292 --> 00:10:35.171
♪ The assurance gives ♪


00:10:35.338 --> 00:10:42.344
♪ I know that my Redeemer ♪


00:10:42.511 --> 00:10:45.724
♪ Lives. ♪


00:11:03.949 --> 00:11:07.578
Steve.


00:11:07.745 --> 00:11:10.539
I do not believe
how that Lachlan talks.


00:11:10.705 --> 00:11:13.834
And did you get that he's a real sir,
like a knight?


00:11:14.001 --> 00:11:16.670
Oh, I mean,
they're just so kind


00:11:16.837 --> 00:11:20.007
and enthusiastic,
but, like, totally polite.


00:11:20.174 --> 00:11:21.632
It's awesome,


00:11:21.799 --> 00:11:24.428
and in that amazing
accent of theirs.


00:11:24.595 --> 00:11:26.804
You're just used to kids, honey.


00:11:26.971 --> 00:11:29.223
Those dudes are old.


00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.726
But, boy, did they love you.


00:11:31.893 --> 00:11:34.187
Whoo!


00:11:34.353 --> 00:11:36.563
And how about you, cowboy?


00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:39.067
That new singing gal is me.


00:11:39.233 --> 00:11:41.611
Do you still love me?


00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:54.956
I loved you when you had
braces on your teeth, Beth.


00:11:55.123 --> 00:11:58.376
And, boy, I love you now.


00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.773
Silver ring, Steve.


00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.192
Silver ring, honey.


00:12:23.192 --> 00:12:25.069
Sometimes I just don't think


00:12:25.236 --> 00:12:27.947
I'm ever...
ever gonna get used to...


00:12:28.114 --> 00:12:30.116
Abstaining?


00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.792
Well, that is the new
Beth Boothby.


00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:43.419
Let's listen
to the old Beth Boothby


00:12:43.586 --> 00:12:45.965
in "Trailer Trash Love."


00:12:46.132 --> 00:12:49.634
♪ I got nothing to sell,
I got favors for rent ♪


00:12:49.801 --> 00:12:53.429
♪ And the lovin' I give
is heaven-sent ♪


00:12:53.596 --> 00:12:55.682
♪ If you buy me a beer
and want to try your luck... ♪


00:12:55.849 --> 00:12:57.308
Oh, no, no.


00:12:57.475 --> 00:13:01.147
♪ Then take me for a ride
in your pickup truck ♪


00:13:01.313 --> 00:13:04.482
♪ Call me cheap,
call me a whore ♪


00:13:04.649 --> 00:13:08.154
♪ That may be true
if you get in my door ♪


00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:12.031
♪ There are pleasures in heaven
from God above ♪


00:13:12.198 --> 00:13:15.659
♪ But, baby, nothing compares
to my trailer trash love... ♪


00:13:17.704 --> 00:13:19.830
Oh, I just hate her.


00:13:19.997 --> 00:13:22.457
But it's you, baby.


00:13:22.624 --> 00:13:25.128
Not any more, she ain't.


00:13:30.716 --> 00:13:32.343
♪ I was born in a car... ♪


00:13:37.306 --> 00:13:39.391
Oh, where are you going, Steve?


00:13:39.558 --> 00:13:41.476
To my room, honey.


00:13:41.643 --> 00:13:45.229
Listen, I promise


00:13:45.396 --> 00:13:47.273
that when we're wed


00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:51.528
you're gonna know you married
a real little old Jezebel.


00:14:05.209 --> 00:14:07.376
Delia.


00:14:07.543 --> 00:14:10.254
Yeah, that concert
was wonderful.


00:14:11.254 --> 00:14:14.425
Oh, you and Lachlan
are so kind.


00:14:14.592 --> 00:14:16.468
No.


00:14:16.635 --> 00:14:19.931
Steve's gotten us a whole bunch
of maps, but thank you.


00:14:21.891 --> 00:14:24.268
Sure, we've got your numbers.


00:14:24.435 --> 00:14:26.770
We'll call if anything comes up.


00:14:26.937 --> 00:14:30.566
Yeah, we'll let you know
how it goes.


00:14:31.733 --> 00:14:34.527
I really appreciate it, Delia.


00:14:34.694 --> 00:14:37.113
'Night.


00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.961
It would make such a difference
if you could just read through these.


00:14:51.127 --> 00:14:53.380
<i>- No, no, no, thank you.
-  If we could just leave them with you.</i>


00:14:53.546 --> 00:14:55.799
- No, no, thank you. No, thank you.
- Please just take...


00:15:11.022 --> 00:15:13.774
And if you just
take a look here at...


00:15:13.941 --> 00:15:15.401
No, no, no.


00:15:15.567 --> 00:15:17.820
If you just let Jesus
into your heart, sir.


00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.041
Those city folk just hated our guts


00:15:32.208 --> 00:15:34.127
- as soon as they saw us.
- Yeah, but...


00:15:34.294 --> 00:15:35.878
A country soul
is as good as a city soul


00:15:36.045 --> 00:15:38.214
any day in my book.
A soul is a soul, Beth.


00:15:38.381 --> 00:15:40.967
And I think we've got a real
good chance to save some,


00:15:41.134 --> 00:15:43.094
- thanks to our friends here.
- Steve's right, Beth.


00:15:43.261 --> 00:15:45.805
What is the point of having
doors slammed in your faces


00:15:45.972 --> 00:15:47.682
by these city people?


00:15:47.849 --> 00:15:49.726
Now, our country neighbors


00:15:49.892 --> 00:15:52.061
may seem like a bunch
of heathens to you,


00:15:52.228 --> 00:15:54.313
but they will hear you out.


00:15:54.479 --> 00:15:56.982
And that I'll promise you.


00:15:58.483 --> 00:16:00.319
Okay.


00:16:00.485 --> 00:16:02.237
Okay, I know we're doing
the right thing.


00:16:02.404 --> 00:16:03.571
And don't for a minute think


00:16:03.738 --> 00:16:06.159
that I'm not real grateful
to y'all for the invite.


00:16:06.326 --> 00:16:10.245
It's just maybe we gave up
on them city folk too soon.


00:16:10.412 --> 00:16:13.832
Forget it.
I'm just being dumb.


00:16:13.999 --> 00:16:15.917
Ain't this a Rolls-Royce?


00:16:16.084 --> 00:16:17.127
No, Steve, sir.


00:16:17.294 --> 00:16:19.462
This is a Hotchkiss.


00:16:19.628 --> 00:16:22.758
On a Rolls, sir,
that figure would be


00:16:22.924 --> 00:16:25.217
the Spirit of Ecstasy.


00:16:25.384 --> 00:16:29.180
But this here is
our goddess Sulis.


00:16:29.346 --> 00:16:32.059
Sir Lachlan
had her made special


00:16:32.225 --> 00:16:35.353
for this classic Hotchkiss,
built 1929,


00:16:35.519 --> 00:16:39.358
as part of his collection
of great cars of the past,


00:16:39.524 --> 00:16:41.025
as you may see.


00:16:41.192 --> 00:16:43.319
Sulis is our
Celtic name for her.


00:16:43.486 --> 00:16:45.403
Of course, the Romans,
when they were here,


00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:46.947
called her Minerva.


00:16:47.114 --> 00:16:49.617
And she doesn't
suffer fools gladly.


00:16:49.784 --> 00:16:53.703
She is the goddess
of the bright, intelligent people


00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.914
we all like to think we are.


00:17:02.797 --> 00:17:06.508
So about this goddess...


00:17:06.674 --> 00:17:09.094
you were kidding, right?


00:17:10.637 --> 00:17:13.473
I take it that both of you
are what you call


00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.557
born again.


00:17:15.724 --> 00:17:16.767
Yeah.


00:17:16.934 --> 00:17:19.646
And do intelligent
people like you believe,


00:17:19.813 --> 00:17:23.065
as 14 million American born again
apparently do,


00:17:23.232 --> 00:17:26.026
that the day Jesus returns,


00:17:26.193 --> 00:17:28.363
everyone who is not born again


00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.407
will bleed to death...


00:17:30.573 --> 00:17:32.408
even innocent children
in Borneo


00:17:32.574 --> 00:17:34.869
who've never even heard
of Jesus?


00:17:36.328 --> 00:17:38.205
Do you believe that?


00:17:38.372 --> 00:17:41.499
Heck, I don't know.


00:17:41.666 --> 00:17:44.586
But if it says so in the Bible,
yes, ma'am,


00:17:44.753 --> 00:17:46.587
because we believe
that everything...


00:17:46.754 --> 00:17:49.424
that every word in the Bible
was inspired by God.


00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:52.094
So it must be true, right?


00:17:53.095 --> 00:17:54.596
Interesting.


00:18:16.325 --> 00:18:18.661
Sir Lachlan.


00:18:24.625 --> 00:18:26.794
Thank you.


00:18:26.961 --> 00:18:28.837
Hello, everybody.


00:18:29.004 --> 00:18:31.674
I'm so glad you two can come.


00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.804
This is going to be fun,
trying to convert us heathens.


00:18:38.971 --> 00:18:41.099
You're quite the famous dude
around here, sir.


00:18:41.266 --> 00:18:42.309
How comes that?


00:18:42.476 --> 00:18:45.687
What makes him famous around here
is that everyone works for him.


00:18:45.854 --> 00:18:48.482
Infamous, more like Monty Burns
in "The Simpsons."


00:18:48.648 --> 00:18:50.984
Anything goes wrong...
I'm usually the villain.


00:19:10.126 --> 00:19:12.756
Morning, Lolly.
How's my Prince today?


00:19:12.923 --> 00:19:15.674
He's been missing you,
Sir Lachlan.


00:19:15.841 --> 00:19:19.093
That's Beth Boothby, isn't it?
Whoa.


00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:22.348
Delia and I are throwing a special party
for her at the manor house on Sunday.


00:19:22.515 --> 00:19:24.724
Everyone's invited,
so spread the word.


00:19:24.891 --> 00:19:27.060
Beth, of course,
is our very special guest.


00:19:27.227 --> 00:19:29.938
Lolly here is our head groom.


00:19:30.104 --> 00:19:32.023
- What a beauty.
- Steve.


00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.442
The horse, Beth.
If that ain't one beautiful horse.


00:19:35.609 --> 00:19:38.197
I'm terribly sorry.
This is Steve.


00:19:38.364 --> 00:19:41.324
As you can see,
he's from America, too.


00:19:42.534 --> 00:19:44.827
- How would you like to ride him?
- I'd like it fine,


00:19:44.994 --> 00:19:46.913
but I think young Beth here
would kill me first.


00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.957
And you'd deserve it.


00:19:49.123 --> 00:19:51.918
You know very well I'm asking Steve
if he'd like to ride Prince.


00:19:52.085 --> 00:19:54.878
Ride that horse?
Are you kidding me? You bet.


00:19:55.045 --> 00:19:57.422
Go on.


00:20:55.145 --> 00:20:57.439
Morning, Jack.


00:20:57.607 --> 00:21:00.276
An American guest for us, Jack.
How about a greeting?


00:21:02.027 --> 00:21:05.448
"Prophet!' say I, 'thing of evil!...


00:21:05.615 --> 00:21:08.199
prophet still,
if bird or devil!...


00:21:08.366 --> 00:21:11.620
On this home,
by horror haunted...


00:21:11.786 --> 00:21:15.123
tell me truly, I implore...


00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.625
ls there...


00:21:16.791 --> 00:21:19.793
is there balm in Gilead?...


00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.796
tell me...


00:21:21.963 --> 00:21:23.797
tell me, I implore!"


00:21:23.964 --> 00:21:25.842
<i>- Nevermore.
-  Whoa.</i>


00:21:26.009 --> 00:21:27.801
Oh, stop showing off, Jack.


00:21:27.968 --> 00:21:29.638
It's one of his party pieces.


00:21:29.804 --> 00:21:31.973
He can't resist
trying it out on strangers.


00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.642
He doesn't really think
you're a prophet.


00:21:34.808 --> 00:21:36.769
We can't understand a word
he's saying half the time,


00:21:36.936 --> 00:21:38.812
- so we call him the Oracle.
- Oracle?


00:21:38.979 --> 00:21:41.440
Yes, it's like a...
like a prophet,


00:21:41.607 --> 00:21:44.400
like Ezekiel in your Bible.


00:21:44.567 --> 00:21:45.986
You're kidding me.


00:21:46.153 --> 00:21:48.404
I probably am,
but don't take offense.


00:21:48.571 --> 00:21:50.782
Now, Steve,


00:21:50.949 --> 00:21:54.703
mindful of your silver rings,
we're splitting you up.


00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.539
Beth will be staying with Mary Hillier,
our housekeeper,


00:21:57.706 --> 00:22:01.502
while you will be left in the capable
hands of Peter McNeill here.


00:22:01.669 --> 00:22:04.587
He'll look after you.
Won't you, Peter?


00:22:06.172 --> 00:22:07.840
Thanks, bud.


00:22:08.007 --> 00:22:10.176
Welcome, Steve.


00:22:10.343 --> 00:22:11.678
Nice to meet you, sir.


00:22:11.844 --> 00:22:13.845
This way.


00:22:21.813 --> 00:22:23.439
Sorry I'm late.


00:22:31.947 --> 00:22:34.741
Bad news, Orlando.
I've got to be back by 8:00.


00:22:34.908 --> 00:22:37.661
8:00? Oh, that's really not fair.
I've arranged the whole outing.


00:22:37.828 --> 00:22:39.787
It's my first evening off
since I've arrived here.


00:22:39.954 --> 00:22:41.372
Come in, come in, Lolly.


00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:43.959
Can't be seen kissing
in the street, not in uniform.


00:22:44.126 --> 00:22:46.503
Oh, well, why don't you
take off the uniform


00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:49.089
and let me see that lovely
Italian body of yours?


00:22:49.256 --> 00:22:51.883
Orlando...


00:22:55.845 --> 00:22:58.807
such a sexy name.


00:22:58.974 --> 00:23:03.269
More sexy than Lolly?
And apart from my granddad,


00:23:03.436 --> 00:23:06.731
I'm as Scottish
as you are, Lolly.


00:23:21.786 --> 00:23:23.706
Let me get this for you, miss.


00:23:23.873 --> 00:23:26.040
Beth.


00:23:26.207 --> 00:23:27.709
That's Mary Hillier,
our housekeeper.


00:23:27.876 --> 00:23:29.753
Oh.


00:23:29.919 --> 00:23:31.504
- Hello. I'm Mary.
- Hi, Mary.


00:23:31.671 --> 00:23:35.008
Welcome, welcome.
Come on, shall I take you in?


00:23:35.175 --> 00:23:36.759
- Yeah.
- Okay. Yes.


00:23:36.925 --> 00:23:40.014
Now this is it.


00:23:40.181 --> 00:23:42.432
So what do you do, Jack,


00:23:42.599 --> 00:23:44.267
aside from feed those birds?


00:23:44.434 --> 00:23:47.604
S-s-sometimes I hunt
for haddocks' eyes


00:23:47.771 --> 00:23:49.981
among the heather bright


00:23:50.148 --> 00:23:54.235
and work them into
waistcoat buttons


00:23:54.402 --> 00:23:56.528
in the silent night.


00:23:56.695 --> 00:23:58.655
My daddy done that.


00:23:58.822 --> 00:24:00.699
He was shitfaced
with moonshine,


00:24:00.866 --> 00:24:03.744
thought I'd turned into some
Godzilla or some darn thing.


00:24:03.911 --> 00:24:05.789
I was lucky the other
five shots missed


00:24:05.955 --> 00:24:08.373
and hit some poor old cow.


00:24:12.628 --> 00:24:14.421
Would you care for a game
of cards, Steve?


00:24:14.588 --> 00:24:16.465
I mean, we only play
for pennies.


00:24:16.632 --> 00:24:19.885
Oh, no, no, no, sir.
I don't gamble no more.


00:24:20.052 --> 00:24:22.970
I used to before I was saved.
I like cards.


00:24:23.137 --> 00:24:25.973
What I really like is to read them
the same as I read the Bible.


00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:28.392
Would you all guys like to see?


00:24:28.559 --> 00:24:31.480
- Of course, yeah.
- Aye.


00:24:31.647 --> 00:24:33.731
Well, when I see the ace,


00:24:33.898 --> 00:24:36.902
it reminds me there is one God.


00:24:37.069 --> 00:24:39.946
And the deuce reminds me


00:24:40.112 --> 00:24:41.989
the Bible's divided
into two parts...


00:24:42.156 --> 00:24:44.033
there's the Old
and the New Testaments.


00:24:44.200 --> 00:24:46.077
And when I see the three,


00:24:46.244 --> 00:24:49.871
I think of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Spirit.


00:24:51.457 --> 00:24:55.168
And when I see the four,


00:24:55.335 --> 00:24:58.547
it reminds me of the four evangelists
who preached the Gospel.


00:24:58.713 --> 00:25:01.384
And the five...


00:25:03.301 --> 00:25:06.263
I think of the five wise virgins
who trimmed their lamps.


00:25:06.429 --> 00:25:08.306
There were 10.
Five were wise and saved.


00:25:08.473 --> 00:25:10.892
Five were foolish and shut out.


00:25:11.059 --> 00:25:13.686
The six...


00:25:13.853 --> 00:25:16.189
I think of the six days
it took God


00:25:16.356 --> 00:25:18.607
to make this great heaven
and this earth.


00:25:18.774 --> 00:25:20.860
And when I see the seven,


00:25:21.026 --> 00:25:23.029
it reminds me
that on the seventh day


00:25:23.196 --> 00:25:25.031
God took His day of rest.


00:25:25.198 --> 00:25:27.033
And when I see the eight,


00:25:27.200 --> 00:25:30.035
I think of the eight
righteous persons God saved


00:25:30.202 --> 00:25:33.498
when He destroyed all on earth.


00:25:34.874 --> 00:25:37.084
With the nine...


00:25:37.251 --> 00:25:40.713
Just a minute. May I?


00:25:43.132 --> 00:25:45.133
Go ahead, bud.


00:26:04.570 --> 00:26:06.154
When I see the nine...


00:26:08.907 --> 00:26:11.701
I think of the lepers
our Savior cleansed,


00:26:11.868 --> 00:26:16.204
and nine out of the 10
didn't even thank Him.


00:26:16.371 --> 00:26:18.374
And when I see the 10,


00:26:18.541 --> 00:26:21.920
I think of the 10 commandments
God handed down to Moses


00:26:22.086 --> 00:26:24.005
on a tablet of stone.


00:26:24.172 --> 00:26:26.506
And when I see the king,


00:26:26.673 --> 00:26:30.802
it reminds me there is but one
King in heaven... God Almighty.


00:26:30.969 --> 00:26:33.180
And when I see the queen,


00:26:33.347 --> 00:26:37.601
I think of the blessed
Virgin Mary, queen of all heaven.


00:26:37.768 --> 00:26:40.270
And the jack...


00:26:40.437 --> 00:26:42.313
why, he's the devil.


00:26:45.777 --> 00:26:47.569
♪ Will you go, laddie, go ♪


00:26:47.736 --> 00:26:49.613
♪ To the braes o'Balquhidder? ♪


00:26:49.780 --> 00:26:51.489
♪ We'll crown the laddie's queen ♪


00:26:51.656 --> 00:26:53.492
♪ And we'll feast the night
together ♪


00:26:53.659 --> 00:26:55.953
♪ Will you go, laddie, go? ♪


00:27:01.582 --> 00:27:03.626
♪ When the spring is in its prime ♪


00:27:03.793 --> 00:27:05.628
♪ And flowers are
freshly blooming ♪


00:27:05.795 --> 00:27:07.629
♪ And the wild mountain thyme ♪


00:27:07.796 --> 00:27:09.632
♪ All the moorland perfuming ♪


00:27:09.799 --> 00:27:12.802
♪ Will you go, laddie, go? ♪


00:27:12.969 --> 00:27:15.012
Oh, my God.


00:27:15.179 --> 00:27:18.891
It really is Beth Boothby.


00:27:19.058 --> 00:27:21.143
Our surprise guest.


00:27:21.310 --> 00:27:22.811
No, Morag.


00:27:22.978 --> 00:27:25.147
Could I?
Could I get a wee autograph?


00:27:25.314 --> 00:27:27.315
It's not for me.
It's for our Johnny.


00:27:27.482 --> 00:27:29.526
He's wild about you.


00:27:29.693 --> 00:27:33.154
That was a real pretty song
you were singing, Morag.


00:27:33.321 --> 00:27:35.448
It's one of our May Day songs.


00:27:35.615 --> 00:27:37.325
Do you celebrate
May Day in America?


00:27:37.491 --> 00:27:39.995
Like the Easter parade?
Chocolate bunnies?


00:27:40.161 --> 00:27:42.039
Not quite.


00:27:42.206 --> 00:27:45.000
Well, Easter's definitely
a big deal in the church...


00:27:45.166 --> 00:27:47.210
you know, Jesus
and the resurrection.


00:27:47.377 --> 00:27:52.007
Our May Day is much much
older than Easter.


00:27:52.173 --> 00:27:55.092
Few Christians realize
that the timing of their Easter


00:27:55.259 --> 00:27:57.137
is controlled by the moon.


00:27:57.303 --> 00:27:59.179
Our goddess.


00:27:59.346 --> 00:28:01.015
May Day is the day
that we celebrate


00:28:01.181 --> 00:28:03.850
the rebirth of everything
in nature...


00:28:04.017 --> 00:28:06.855
the blossoming trees,
the new crops,


00:28:07.022 --> 00:28:11.025
the sap rising
in our own bodies.


00:28:11.191 --> 00:28:14.153
Do you not feel it?


00:28:16.363 --> 00:28:19.282
Would you like to see
the May Queen's dress we're making?


00:28:19.449 --> 00:28:20.826
I'd love to.


00:28:20.993 --> 00:28:24.912
Would you like to try it on?
You'd be the first to wear it.


00:28:25.079 --> 00:28:26.998
- Really?
- Uh-huh.


00:28:30.084 --> 00:28:32.629
Oh, wow.


00:28:32.796 --> 00:28:35.631
♪ The light lilting chorus ♪


00:28:35.798 --> 00:28:38.343
♪ Will you go, laddie, go? ♪


00:28:38.510 --> 00:28:40.386
Can I see it?


00:28:40.553 --> 00:28:42.388
Okay.


00:28:42.555 --> 00:28:44.723
Oh, wow.


00:28:47.226 --> 00:28:49.311
This is the coolest dress.


00:28:49.478 --> 00:28:53.441
Oh, you guys are so clever.


00:28:53.608 --> 00:28:56.568
I wish y'all could make something
for my next gig.


00:28:56.735 --> 00:28:59.197
I'm being really selfish.


00:28:59.363 --> 00:29:02.283
Why don't y'all try it on?


00:29:02.450 --> 00:29:04.743
The May Queen is elected, Beth.


00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:08.246
No one tries on the queen's dress
except the queen.


00:29:08.413 --> 00:29:10.749
We made an exception
for you, Beth,


00:29:10.916 --> 00:29:13.293
because I happen to know
that Lachlan and Delia


00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:16.462
rather hope you'll consent to be
the May Queen yourself.


00:29:18.048 --> 00:29:19.424
I shouldn't have told you that,


00:29:19.591 --> 00:29:21.592
'cause I know they want
to ask you themselves.


00:29:56.209 --> 00:29:58.087
Orlando!


00:29:58.254 --> 00:30:00.798
Orgasissimo!


00:30:00.965 --> 00:30:03.675
Oh!


00:30:05.135 --> 00:30:07.762
Whew.


00:30:07.929 --> 00:30:10.473
Five times?


00:30:11.474 --> 00:30:13.893
Sure.


00:30:15.228 --> 00:30:17.479
Why not


00:30:17.647 --> 00:30:19.858
seven?


00:30:20.024 --> 00:30:22.235
I'm sure you, Orlando,
could do it.


00:30:22.402 --> 00:30:25.155
Italian men are
such wonderful lovers.


00:30:25.321 --> 00:30:28.490
What a great idea.


00:30:28.657 --> 00:30:30.577
Are you on?


00:30:30.743 --> 00:30:32.369
Nobody would touch that record.


00:30:32.536 --> 00:30:34.413
You keep records here?


00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:36.498
No, not really.


00:30:36.665 --> 00:30:39.293
Well, quite informally.


00:30:42.254 --> 00:30:44.756
You really are a treat, Orlando.


00:30:50.179 --> 00:30:52.055
Scots and Englishmen


00:30:52.222 --> 00:30:54.349
can always find their way
to the pub,


00:30:54.516 --> 00:30:56.685
but when it comes
to the clitoris,


00:30:56.852 --> 00:31:00.605
they think it's an island off Greece
famous for its ouzo.


00:31:01.898 --> 00:31:05.651
♪ Bonny lads 0' Gala Water ♪


00:31:05.818 --> 00:31:09.863
♪ I'll kilt my skirt
upon my knee... ♪


00:31:14.410 --> 00:31:18.206
♪ I tempted him with apples ♪


00:31:18.372 --> 00:31:22.460
♪ All golden in the light ♪


00:31:22.627 --> 00:31:25.962
♪ He laid me in the orchard ♪


00:31:26.129 --> 00:31:30.008
♪ Till the day turned
into night ♪


00:31:30.175 --> 00:31:33.595
♪ And since he plucked
my cherry ♪


00:31:33.761 --> 00:31:37.390
♪ All juicy, red and ripe ♪


00:31:37.558 --> 00:31:40.977
♪ He sampled all the berries ♪


00:31:41.144 --> 00:31:44.731
♪ Till the taste of me he won ♪


00:31:44.898 --> 00:31:48.151
♪ A tryst is in the forest ♪


00:31:48.318 --> 00:31:51.821
♪ Where no one else will come ♪


00:31:51.988 --> 00:31:55.741
♪ And he don't want
any gooseberries ♪


00:31:55.908 --> 00:31:59.412
♪ A-spoiling all our fun ♪


00:31:59.578 --> 00:32:03.707
♪ Oh, the fruits
of the forest ♪


00:32:03.874 --> 00:32:07.879
♪ And the fruits of the tree ♪


00:32:08.046 --> 00:32:11.590
♪ I'll give to my love... ♪


00:32:50.877 --> 00:32:53.130
Steve.


00:32:53.297 --> 00:32:56.133
Steve, wake up.


00:32:57.509 --> 00:33:00.638
- Good morning, Steve.
- Good morning, sir.


00:33:00.805 --> 00:33:02.264
You remember Prince?


00:33:02.431 --> 00:33:04.851
We thought you might like
to look around the countryside,


00:33:05.018 --> 00:33:06.893
so we brought him along
for you to ride.


00:33:07.060 --> 00:33:09.396
All right!
I'll be right down.


00:33:14.776 --> 00:33:16.445
So which way, ma'am?


00:33:16.610 --> 00:33:18.779
If I were you, I'd take him
to the old castle...


00:33:18.946 --> 00:33:20.949
left at the end,
over the bridge,


00:33:21.116 --> 00:33:23.200
follow the river.


00:33:23.367 --> 00:33:25.787
You might want to shorten
those stirrups a bit, Steve.


00:33:25.954 --> 00:33:28.874
Oh, no, no, no, ma'am.
I always ride like this.


00:33:29.041 --> 00:33:31.084
Thank you very much.


00:33:33.336 --> 00:33:35.379
Morning.


00:33:39.216 --> 00:33:40.968
He's going to the castle.


00:33:41.135 --> 00:33:42.927
He won't get far.


00:33:45.723 --> 00:33:47.974
Whoa.
Down, boy. Down, boy.


00:34:16.544 --> 00:34:19.506
Ah, Steve.


00:34:19.672 --> 00:34:22.592
So what do you think of Prince
now you've ridden him?


00:34:22.759 --> 00:34:25.178
Awesome.
That's one real special horse.


00:34:26.721 --> 00:34:29.306
The Anthea lady...
she warned me about the stirrups.


00:34:29.473 --> 00:34:31.725
I nearly hit the dirt
back there.


00:34:31.892 --> 00:34:34.728
- Why don't you come for a swim?
- Oh, I really can't do that.


00:34:34.895 --> 00:34:36.897
Sulis is real welcoming
this morning.


00:34:37.064 --> 00:34:40.024
It'll make your skin feel velvety.


00:34:41.235 --> 00:34:43.570
It's giving me good vibes.


00:34:45.280 --> 00:34:47.324
I just can't believe
this is for real.


00:34:48.618 --> 00:34:50.619
You want me to come in?


00:34:54.705 --> 00:34:56.834
Oh, what the hell?


00:35:00.211 --> 00:35:03.506
Sulis... ain't that
some kind of goddess?


00:35:03.673 --> 00:35:05.007
How did you know that?


00:35:05.174 --> 00:35:07.385
I saw her on the front
of Lachlan's vehicle.


00:35:07.552 --> 00:35:09.178
She's cute.


00:35:09.345 --> 00:35:11.514
I'm glad you approved of her.


00:35:11.681 --> 00:35:13.600
I posed for the wee statue.


00:35:13.767 --> 00:35:15.935
It was a great honor.


00:35:17.103 --> 00:35:19.647
This is Sulis's sacred spring.


00:35:33.243 --> 00:35:36.746
Wow, Sulis.


00:35:39.667 --> 00:35:41.543
You gotta be kidding me
about this.


00:35:41.710 --> 00:35:43.587
This is just some
warm water, right?


00:35:43.753 --> 00:35:47.132
You believe a certain virgin
had a baby, don't you?


00:35:47.299 --> 00:35:49.134
Why can't you believe, like I do,


00:35:49.301 --> 00:35:52.636
that this water has a holy power?


00:35:52.803 --> 00:35:56.140
I believe whatever's written
in the Bible, Lolly.


00:35:56.307 --> 00:35:58.142
That's Holy Writ.


00:35:59.477 --> 00:36:01.729
Come on, Steve.


00:36:01.896 --> 00:36:04.274
It'll make you feel
out of this world.


00:36:10.071 --> 00:36:12.281
Are you thinking about Beth?


00:36:12.448 --> 00:36:15.284
I can let you into a secret.


00:36:15.451 --> 00:36:19.455
Lachlan wants her
to be the May Queen.


00:36:19.622 --> 00:36:22.332
I think he might like you to be
the Laddie. Would you go for that?


00:36:22.499 --> 00:36:23.583
What's the Laddie?


00:36:23.750 --> 00:36:27.253
The Laddie?
You've not heard tell of the Laddie?


00:36:27.420 --> 00:36:29.714
He is the brightest


00:36:29.881 --> 00:36:32.175
and best,


00:36:32.342 --> 00:36:35.012
the handsomest,


00:36:35.179 --> 00:36:37.514
the kindest, the goodest,


00:36:37.680 --> 00:36:40.183
perhaps the best rider.


00:36:45.939 --> 00:36:49.859
I have known him to be
the best lover.


00:37:16.260 --> 00:37:19.554
I never dreamed
it could be like that.


00:37:19.720 --> 00:37:23.183
Think it might go on
forever and ever.


00:37:23.349 --> 00:37:25.811
Kind of hoping it would.


00:37:27.229 --> 00:37:30.816
I always look for something


00:37:30.983 --> 00:37:33.526
that I know
even Sulis cannot give me...


00:37:37.990 --> 00:37:40.366
a child.


00:37:40.533 --> 00:37:42.952
But I know
that if it does happen,


00:37:43.119 --> 00:37:45.579
it will have happened here.


00:37:50.041 --> 00:37:52.378
What do you mean, "always"?


00:37:53.963 --> 00:37:58.175
Well, I am what the goddess
wants me to be...


00:37:59.217 --> 00:38:01.845
all things to all men.


00:38:05.599 --> 00:38:08.768
We've got a word for that
back in Texas, yeah,


00:38:08.935 --> 00:38:11.313
and it ain't pretty.


00:38:18.236 --> 00:38:20.322
Still,


00:38:20.488 --> 00:38:23.450
I reckon somehow
you're different.


00:38:23.617 --> 00:38:25.784
I'm glad.


00:38:35.461 --> 00:38:36.587
Lost something?


00:38:36.754 --> 00:38:38.631
Yeah.


00:38:38.797 --> 00:38:41.132
I guess it don't matter no more.


00:38:42.926 --> 00:38:45.471
You lost it, you lost it.


00:38:46.764 --> 00:38:48.807
Ain't no going back.


00:38:52.311 --> 00:38:54.813
Here comes the big,
unreadable book


00:38:54.980 --> 00:38:56.898
that's supposed to
explain everything?


00:38:57.065 --> 00:38:59.610
A big pile of these in the house...
I used them as a doorstop.


00:38:59.777 --> 00:39:01.819
- Now, what we have here


00:39:01.986 --> 00:39:04.989
is the latest report on what we've done
in the 10 years since the accident


00:39:05.156 --> 00:39:08.451
to make our environment
entirely secure.


00:39:08.618 --> 00:39:10.871
Naturally, you will have
some questions,


00:39:11.038 --> 00:39:12.789
but I asked you here to rebut


00:39:12.955 --> 00:39:15.918
some absolutely untrue
reports in the press.


00:39:16.085 --> 00:39:17.126
Yes, Patricia.


00:39:17.293 --> 00:39:19.921
You've been protesting
about my piece in "The Ecologist"


00:39:20.088 --> 00:39:22.339
with which Magnus
absolutely concurs,


00:39:22.506 --> 00:39:26.177
so will you not just agree
that nuclear is just too expensive


00:39:26.344 --> 00:39:30.013
and just too damned dangerous
to live nearby?


00:39:30.180 --> 00:39:32.015
Patricia,


00:39:32.182 --> 00:39:34.851
the greatest power station
in our solar system


00:39:35.018 --> 00:39:36.977
is dangerous... the sun.


00:39:37.144 --> 00:39:40.191
It creates deserts,
melts icecaps,


00:39:40.358 --> 00:39:43.151
causes cancer.
We've been living with it


00:39:43.318 --> 00:39:46.238
since our ancestors crawled out
of the primeval slime.


00:39:48.031 --> 00:39:51.535
Respect and understanding
for these forces of nature


00:39:51.702 --> 00:39:54.995
is the key to controlling them,
Patricia.


00:39:55.162 --> 00:39:57.207
Nuclear is just one of them.


00:39:57.373 --> 00:39:59.709
I'm convener here for my union.


00:39:59.875 --> 00:40:01.752
Do you think I'd risk
my members' lives?


00:40:01.919 --> 00:40:03.796
Can I quote you


00:40:03.963 --> 00:40:07.134
on your "slimy ancestors,"
Sir Lachlan?


00:40:07.300 --> 00:40:09.885
Yes, of course.


00:40:10.052 --> 00:40:13.597
Patricia said we're the best
double act since Laurel and Hardy.


00:40:15.850 --> 00:40:18.059
After the accident,
the press went on


00:40:18.226 --> 00:40:20.563
about the danger
of a nuclear catastrophe.


00:40:20.730 --> 00:40:24.107
Funny that they never do
their homework.


00:40:24.274 --> 00:40:25.775
A river is a river,


00:40:25.942 --> 00:40:27.987
but the water table
is another thing.


00:40:28.154 --> 00:40:30.321
One flows.
The other is static.


00:40:30.488 --> 00:40:32.283
Journalists...
thank heavens they have


00:40:32.450 --> 00:40:34.242
the attention span of wet hens.


00:40:34.409 --> 00:40:37.288
The accident did poison the water table.
Now the villagers are infertile.


00:40:37.455 --> 00:40:40.999
Sick babies they might notice,
even deformed babies.


00:40:41.166 --> 00:40:43.877
But virtually no babies...
no comment


00:40:44.043 --> 00:40:46.588
so far.


00:40:58.266 --> 00:41:01.227
We have come a long way


00:41:01.394 --> 00:41:03.772
to remind you folks
about Jesus,


00:41:03.938 --> 00:41:07.483
because I just know
you've already heard about Him,


00:41:07.649 --> 00:41:09.526
just like you've heard about.


00:41:09.693 --> 00:41:12.529
Rob Roy or Braveheart


00:41:12.696 --> 00:41:15.281
or Mr. Bell...
the great Scottish man


00:41:15.448 --> 00:41:17.201
who gave us all the telephone.


00:41:17.367 --> 00:41:20.286
It's just many of you
may have forgotten


00:41:20.453 --> 00:41:22.955
that Jesus was braver
than Rob Roy


00:41:23.122 --> 00:41:25.876
because He gave His life
for all of us,


00:41:26.043 --> 00:41:28.462
and not just the people
of His time,


00:41:28.629 --> 00:41:30.880
but the people of all time.


00:41:31.047 --> 00:41:32.925
And you may have forgotten


00:41:33.091 --> 00:41:36.219
that Jesus was not
just a great inventor,


00:41:36.385 --> 00:41:38.304
He was the greatest of all


00:41:38.471 --> 00:41:41.974
because He invented
a new kind of love.


00:41:42.141 --> 00:41:45.685
Now, what was that, friends?
Can any of you remember?


00:41:45.852 --> 00:41:48.981
It is love of everyone
but yourself...


00:41:49.148 --> 00:41:52.485
really hard,
wouldn't you agree, Beth?


00:41:52.652 --> 00:41:55.904
Delia, that is
such a good question.


00:41:56.071 --> 00:41:58.825
And I see Steve would like
to answer you.


00:41:58.991 --> 00:42:00.867
No, ma'am, no.


00:42:01.034 --> 00:42:03.620
If you can love other folks


00:42:03.787 --> 00:42:06.581
like Jesus loves us,


00:42:06.748 --> 00:42:09.835
then there's no other reason
to love yourself.


00:42:10.001 --> 00:42:11.877
'Cause you're so full of love,


00:42:12.044 --> 00:42:15.048
you're like some
great, big light.


00:42:15.215 --> 00:42:17.132
- Like a beacon?
- Right.


00:42:17.299 --> 00:42:19.845
And like Jesus.


00:42:20.011 --> 00:42:23.723
Now, friends, I'd like
to ask Steve to pass among you.


00:42:23.890 --> 00:42:26.767
And he'll be handing out
some thoughts on Jesus


00:42:26.934 --> 00:42:28.979
that we'd like you to read
real closely


00:42:29.145 --> 00:42:32.231
and also some real pretty hymns
for us to sing together.


00:42:32.398 --> 00:42:34.567
Now, please, friends,


00:42:34.733 --> 00:42:37.194
the hymns' words
are real important.


00:42:37.361 --> 00:42:41.073
Just try and believe
what you're singing


00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:43.658
and you'll open your hearts
to Jesus.


