00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:53.650
♪ Will you go, laddie, go? ♪


00:46:53.817 --> 00:46:56.153
♪ Will you go, laddie, go ♪


00:46:56.320 --> 00:46:59.322
♪ To the braes
o'Balquhidder? ♪


00:46:59.489 --> 00:47:01.491
♪ We'll crown the laddie's queen ♪


00:47:01.658 --> 00:47:03.952
♪ And we'll feast the night
together ♪


00:47:04.119 --> 00:47:09.081
♪ Will you go, laddie, go? ♪


00:47:09.248 --> 00:47:12.461
And here, to crown the queen,


00:47:12.628 --> 00:47:14.796
is her Laddie.


00:47:20.844 --> 00:47:24.180
This used to
be a hunting lodge once.


00:47:24.347 --> 00:47:27.517
Oh, but they tried
to ban all that.


00:47:27.684 --> 00:47:30.853
Fishing will be next, they say.


00:47:31.019 --> 00:47:33.480
Too painful
for the poor wee fish.


00:47:50.038 --> 00:47:51.915
There.


00:47:52.082 --> 00:47:54.293
This will be
nice and cozy for you.


00:47:54.459 --> 00:47:57.461
We thought you'd like
a wee moment to yourselves,


00:47:57.628 --> 00:47:59.630
my lambs.


00:48:02.466 --> 00:48:06.554
So, some punch to celebrate.


00:48:06.721 --> 00:48:11.017
Now, Delia will be here
to collect our queen a little later.


00:48:11.184 --> 00:48:13.394
And Sir Lachlan is coming by
with Prince, laddie,


00:48:13.561 --> 00:48:16.397
to go rehearse
for your ride tomorrow.


00:48:16.564 --> 00:48:19.275
It was better than I could
have dreamed, wasn't it, Mary?


00:48:19.442 --> 00:48:21.568
They loved you, my lambs.


00:48:21.735 --> 00:48:23.612
Couldn't you tell?


00:48:23.778 --> 00:48:27.240
We all thought you
were just perfect.


00:48:27.407 --> 00:48:29.284
You're just so kind.


00:48:29.451 --> 00:48:31.245
Oh.


00:48:47.593 --> 00:48:50.430
You have a problem, Steve?


00:48:50.597 --> 00:48:53.432
I mean, wasn't that a triumph


00:48:53.599 --> 00:48:55.935
beyond our wildest dreams?


00:48:56.101 --> 00:48:58.605
Sure,


00:48:58.772 --> 00:49:00.941
in some weird way, I guess.


00:49:02.608 --> 00:49:04.611
Steve.


00:49:05.946 --> 00:49:07.947
Steve.


00:49:11.992 --> 00:49:14.078
I want out, Beth.


00:49:14.245 --> 00:49:16.121
I don't mean tomorrow.


00:49:16.288 --> 00:49:18.289
I'll do the Laddie bit
like they've asked.


00:49:18.456 --> 00:49:20.542
I'll stay and I'll watch them
crown you and all.


00:49:20.709 --> 00:49:22.919
But after that,


00:49:23.086 --> 00:49:25.839
I'm high tailing it home.


00:49:26.006 --> 00:49:29.426
I'm just a dumb cowboy, Beth.


00:49:29.593 --> 00:49:32.638
I mean, this ain't me.


00:49:33.638 --> 00:49:35.890
I just want out.


00:49:36.057 --> 00:49:37.726
Out?


00:49:39.394 --> 00:49:42.814
You can't mean that, Steve.


00:49:42.981 --> 00:49:45.233
You're a redeemer like me.


00:49:45.400 --> 00:49:48.568
You can't suddenly run out
on what that means.


00:49:51.572 --> 00:49:53.825
What is it?


00:49:53.992 --> 00:49:55.952
Tell me.


00:49:56.119 --> 00:49:58.454
Something happened?


00:50:02.750 --> 00:50:05.669
I know what I do well, Beth...


00:50:05.836 --> 00:50:08.338
ride a horse.


00:50:08.505 --> 00:50:11.508
I'm not worthy to be
no redeemer.


00:50:13.010 --> 00:50:15.177
No ways.


00:50:17.222 --> 00:50:19.349
I'm a sinner,


00:50:19.516 --> 00:50:21.518
big time.


00:50:22.686 --> 00:50:26.231
About what happened
in that hotel in Edinburgh


00:50:26.398 --> 00:50:29.942
when we suddenly thought
about our silver rings?


00:50:32.194 --> 00:50:34.531
Steve,


00:50:34.697 --> 00:50:37.074
where's your ring?


00:50:39.327 --> 00:50:41.329
I lost it.


00:50:43.539 --> 00:50:46.959
I'm not the guy for you, Beth.


00:50:50.129 --> 00:50:54.091
Can you be a believer
and a sinner?


00:50:54.258 --> 00:50:56.134
I guess you can't,


00:50:56.301 --> 00:50:58.721
'cause that's me.


00:51:00.764 --> 00:51:02.640
I'm real sorry, Beth.


00:51:02.807 --> 00:51:05.518
Please forgive me.


00:51:13.611 --> 00:51:16.071
Tomorrow I'll be the Laddie.


00:51:16.237 --> 00:51:19.115
And after that
hopefully we'll... we'll...


00:51:19.282 --> 00:51:22.285
we'll gather in a whole wagonload
of souls for Jesus.


00:51:22.452 --> 00:51:24.829
Then I'm gonna go back home


00:51:24.996 --> 00:51:27.247
to Texas where I belong.


00:51:27.414 --> 00:51:30.210
And I so hope
you'll come with me, baby.


00:52:05.828 --> 00:52:07.662
Now, the thing to remember


00:52:07.829 --> 00:52:10.582
is don't let them trap you
before you get to the castle.


00:52:10.749 --> 00:52:12.625
Keep your eyes open.
Keep watching


00:52:12.792 --> 00:52:15.253
180°, 360 if you can.


00:52:15.420 --> 00:52:17.046
They can come
from any direction.


00:52:17.213 --> 00:52:20.967
Thanks to Prince,
you can always outride them.


00:52:21.134 --> 00:52:24.594
Oh, and one more thing:


00:52:24.761 --> 00:52:27.515
Don't let anyone tell you
which way to ride.


00:52:27.682 --> 00:52:29.933
It's an old trick.


00:52:30.100 --> 00:52:32.437
So if I win,


00:52:32.603 --> 00:52:34.814
what happens next?


00:52:34.981 --> 00:52:38.191
Well, inside there's an ancient chair
made of stone.


00:52:38.358 --> 00:52:40.277
That's the Laddie's throne.


00:52:40.444 --> 00:52:42.320
You sit there


00:52:42.488 --> 00:52:44.489
and we'll come for you.


00:52:47.784 --> 00:52:50.202
Does it piss you off, sir,
that I figure


00:52:50.369 --> 00:52:52.873
you guys are out of your minds
with this Laddie thing?


00:52:55.082 --> 00:52:57.418
Does it matter to you
that you think that?


00:52:57.586 --> 00:53:01.131
Getting to ride Prince...
that's a prize in itself.


00:53:01.298 --> 00:53:03.508
No, sir.
It's cool with me.


00:53:03.674 --> 00:53:06.343
Well, Steve,
if it's cool with you,


00:53:06.510 --> 00:53:09.513
it's cool with me.


00:53:25.029 --> 00:53:28.532
♪ I got nothing to sell,
I got favors for rent ♪


00:53:28.699 --> 00:53:32.328
♪ And the lovin' I give
is heaven-sent ♪


00:53:32.495 --> 00:53:35.872
♪ If you buy me a beer
and want to try your luck ♪


00:53:36.039 --> 00:53:40.043
♪ Then take me for a ride
in your pickup truck ♪


00:53:40.210 --> 00:53:42.837
♪ Call me cheap,
call me... ♪


00:53:58.561 --> 00:54:00.979
Laddie, can I have
your autograph?


00:54:01.146 --> 00:54:03.566
You sure can.


00:54:06.401 --> 00:54:08.195
What's your name, bud?


00:54:08.362 --> 00:54:10.571
Angus McClintock.
But just write "To Angus."


00:54:10.738 --> 00:54:14.576
Okay. Hey, you're the only kid
I see around here. How come?


00:54:14.743 --> 00:54:16.577
There aren't very many kids
around here.


00:54:16.744 --> 00:54:18.956
Right on. You want me to sign
myself just "Laddie"


00:54:19.122 --> 00:54:21.124
or you want my real name?


00:54:21.291 --> 00:54:22.876
Both, please, Laddie.


00:54:23.043 --> 00:54:25.212
Angus, shouldn't you be
at home?


00:54:25.379 --> 00:54:27.923
Laddie, are you a cowboy?
I mean, for real?


00:54:28.090 --> 00:54:29.132
I sure am.


00:54:29.299 --> 00:54:31.592
So where are your shooters, then?


00:54:31.759 --> 00:54:33.594
Go on, Angus.
You're bothering the Laddie.


00:54:33.761 --> 00:54:35.430
Get on home
before I call your dad.


00:54:35.597 --> 00:54:36.764
No, Pete, it's cool.


00:54:36.931 --> 00:54:39.225
I left my shooters
back home in Texas


00:54:39.392 --> 00:54:42.185
'cause those airlines... they don't
like me having them on the plane.


00:54:42.352 --> 00:54:44.231
Thanks for the autograph, Laddie.


00:54:44.398 --> 00:54:45.983
I just wish you'd
brought your shooters.


00:54:46.149 --> 00:54:48.025
You really could have
used them tomorrow.


00:54:48.192 --> 00:54:50.820
Angus, I'll call your dad.


00:54:57.033 --> 00:55:01.289
Ah, so that is what the modern
missionaries are wearing these days.


00:55:01.455 --> 00:55:04.291
Or are you trying
to tell us something, Beth?


00:55:04.457 --> 00:55:07.293
Okay, I'll admit it.


00:55:07.459 --> 00:55:09.588
I'm mad as hell at Steve.


00:55:09.754 --> 00:55:12.299
But you're throwing a party for me
and I plan to enjoy it.


00:55:13.550 --> 00:55:15.970
Carla made the dress for me
to wear after a gig.


00:55:16.137 --> 00:55:18.138
I don't know why I packed it.


00:55:18.305 --> 00:55:20.515
It must have been
a premonition.


00:55:20.682 --> 00:55:23.392
So do you plan
to forgive Steve?


00:55:23.559 --> 00:55:24.936
Say, tomorrow?


00:55:25.103 --> 00:55:27.646
You must remember
to err is human,


00:55:27.813 --> 00:55:30.107
to forgive... divine.


00:55:30.274 --> 00:55:32.776
I'll probably forgive him
in half an hour.


00:55:32.943 --> 00:55:34.987
You know why?


00:55:35.154 --> 00:55:37.490
Because I love
that son of a bitch cowboy.


00:57:04.950 --> 00:57:07.076
♪ The feast shall cloy not ♪


00:57:07.243 --> 00:57:10.538
♪ Nor the chase shall tire ♪


00:57:12.123 --> 00:57:15.334
♪ Nor music cease forever ♪


00:57:15.500 --> 00:57:19.046
♪ Through the hall ♪


00:57:20.047 --> 00:57:22.215
♪ The gold and jewels ♪


00:57:22.382 --> 00:57:26.595
♪ Of the Land of Youth ♪


00:57:26.762 --> 00:57:29.265
♪ Outshine all splendors ♪


00:57:29.432 --> 00:57:33.227
♪ Ever dreamed by man ♪


00:57:33.394 --> 00:57:36.438
♪ Thou shalt have horses ♪


00:57:36.604 --> 00:57:41.025
♪ Of the fairy breed ♪


00:57:41.192 --> 00:57:43.611
♪ Thou shalt have hounds ♪


00:57:43.778 --> 00:57:47.906
♪ That can outrun the wind ♪


00:57:48.073 --> 00:57:50.786
♪ A hundred chiefs ♪


00:57:50.953 --> 00:57:54.622
♪ Shall follow thee in war... ♪


00:57:54.789 --> 00:57:56.999
Dear God...


00:57:57.166 --> 00:58:00.295
I've got to get this
in the right order.


00:58:02.296 --> 00:58:05.048
Thank you, as always,


00:58:05.215 --> 00:58:07.384
for my wonderful voice


00:58:07.551 --> 00:58:10.763
and for making me
so okay-looking.


00:58:10.929 --> 00:58:14.308
And thank you for making
that amazing prayer meeting


00:58:14.475 --> 00:58:16.477
such a success.


00:58:16.643 --> 00:58:19.313
And, God,


00:58:19.480 --> 00:58:22.192
Steve...


00:58:22.357 --> 00:58:24.568
I want him back.


00:58:24.735 --> 00:58:27.362
I know that you help those
that help themselves.


00:58:27.528 --> 00:58:30.657
And I guess I didn't use
my womanly wiles


00:58:30.824 --> 00:58:33.159
any too wisely
where Steve is concerned.


00:58:33.326 --> 00:58:35.661
But, please, God,


00:58:35.828 --> 00:58:37.997
rekindle in Steve's heart


00:58:38.164 --> 00:58:40.666
the love that he used to
have for me.


00:58:40.833 --> 00:58:43.502
Amen.


00:58:43.668 --> 00:58:45.964
- Who is it?


00:58:46.131 --> 00:58:48.508
It's me, miss,
with your hot milk.


00:58:48.674 --> 00:58:50.968
Come in.


00:59:07.067 --> 00:59:09.109
Just there.


00:59:15.575 --> 00:59:17.202
Magog, Magog.


00:59:17.369 --> 00:59:19.955
- Come here, come here.
- No, no, no, no, leave him, please.


00:59:20.121 --> 00:59:21.998
I like cats.


00:59:22.165 --> 00:59:24.041
Very good, miss,
if you're sure.


00:59:24.208 --> 00:59:27.212
I'm sure. Thanks.


00:59:37.722 --> 00:59:39.723
Good night.


00:59:41.058 --> 00:59:43.436
Good night, miss.


01:00:05.248 --> 01:00:07.418
That's not for you, Magog.


01:00:07.585 --> 01:00:09.587
It's too hot.


01:00:34.944 --> 01:00:37.362
- Sitting astride a horse all day


01:00:37.529 --> 01:00:39.949
makes me horny as hell
sometimes.


01:00:41.533 --> 01:00:44.620
Oh, here, let me help you
off with that.


01:00:51.542 --> 01:00:53.544
That was number six.


01:00:53.711 --> 01:00:56.131
Lolly, you said
you were gonna tell me


01:00:56.298 --> 01:00:58.342
about that cult that's been
reported around here


01:00:58.508 --> 01:01:00.510
if we got to six.


01:01:00.677 --> 01:01:04.640
Seven.
I said seven.


01:01:06.141 --> 01:01:09.518
Seven is going to be
the best yet.


01:01:10.645 --> 01:01:12.480
Of course,


01:01:12.647 --> 01:01:16.525
everybody knows about
the old great scarf act.


01:01:16.692 --> 01:01:19.862
I'm sure you do...


01:01:21.155 --> 01:01:24.492
but not the way I do it.


01:01:27.703 --> 01:01:29.580
Lolly's latest...


01:01:29.747 --> 01:01:32.499
Orlando Orgasissimo.


01:02:22.881 --> 01:02:25.718
Lolly's hospitalized
the copper.


01:02:25.884 --> 01:02:29.554
Well, I'm afraid we have not been
successful with Beth.


01:02:30.972 --> 01:02:33.017
Magog is dead.


01:02:38.187 --> 01:02:40.273
Must have got to the milk.


01:02:40.440 --> 01:02:43.818
Beth, however,
seems to be all right.


01:02:43.985 --> 01:02:46.988
Well, Beame, you'd better deal
with Miss Beth after breakfast,


01:02:47.155 --> 01:02:48.699
give her a shot of the usual.


01:02:48.866 --> 01:02:51.451
Yes, sir.


01:02:51.617 --> 01:02:54.620
Beg pardon, sir,
what if she's awake?


01:02:54.786 --> 01:02:57.123
Then put her to sleep.


01:02:58.249 --> 01:03:00.917
Good God, man,
how long have we been doing this?


01:03:01.084 --> 01:03:03.378
Oh, pity about Magog.


01:03:03.545 --> 01:03:05.422
We will miss him.


01:03:05.589 --> 01:03:07.257
Yes, well, the mice won't.


01:03:08.925 --> 01:03:12.680
Beame, get her ready for tomorrow
before there are any more mishaps.


01:03:12.847 --> 01:03:14.474
Yes, Sir Lachlan.


01:03:14.640 --> 01:03:16.349
Get cook to help you.


01:03:16.516 --> 01:03:18.727
Daisy always frets a bit.


01:03:18.894 --> 01:03:22.564
She doesn't really like
helping me.


01:03:22.731 --> 01:03:26.192
"Gruesome" was
the word she used.


01:03:26.358 --> 01:03:30.113
Oh, well, the weaker sex.


01:03:32.615 --> 01:03:35.034
Although not of course you,


01:03:35.201 --> 01:03:37.579
my lady.


01:03:46.420 --> 01:03:49.131
Mary Hillier asked me
an odd question yesterday.


01:03:49.298 --> 01:03:51.133
She wondered, do I...


01:03:51.299 --> 01:03:55.012
do you really believe


01:03:55.179 --> 01:03:57.639
in what you've led us
to believe?


01:03:58.640 --> 01:04:00.976
Hmm, yes.


01:04:01.143 --> 01:04:03.311
It's a very good question.


01:04:03.478 --> 01:04:06.190
Am I a sincere believer?


01:04:18.993 --> 01:04:22.121
Why have you put in the Laddie?


01:04:22.287 --> 01:04:24.873
Oh, it's you.


01:04:25.041 --> 01:04:27.085
I've always wanted
to paint the bridge.


01:04:27.251 --> 01:04:29.253
And then I thought,


01:04:29.419 --> 01:04:31.756
"imagine the whole of Tressock


01:04:31.923 --> 01:04:33.967
will be riding after the Laddie."


01:04:34.134 --> 01:04:36.469
Poor wee Laddie.


01:04:36.636 --> 01:04:38.846
That bridge has seen so much drama


01:04:39.012 --> 01:04:40.597
over the past few centuries.


01:04:40.764 --> 01:04:44.601
Poor wee Laddie.


01:04:44.768 --> 01:04:46.645
Hunting him


01:04:46.812 --> 01:04:49.189
is a game of chance.


01:04:49.356 --> 01:04:51.733
You've often said


01:04:51.900 --> 01:04:54.068
that what you believe in


01:04:54.235 --> 01:04:56.445
is the natural order of things...


01:04:56.612 --> 01:04:58.490
the food chain.


01:04:58.657 --> 01:05:01.160
Cruel or benign,


01:05:01.326 --> 01:05:03.202
for you,


01:05:03.369 --> 01:05:05.664
everything under the sun happens


01:05:05.831 --> 01:05:08.000
because it just happens.


01:05:08.167 --> 01:05:09.750
That's fate.


01:05:09.917 --> 01:05:13.379
But can fate be altered?


01:05:13.546 --> 01:05:15.882
This is a question


01:05:16.048 --> 01:05:19.217
that every religion
have tried to answer.


01:05:19.384 --> 01:05:22.972
And the answer is
almost certainly no.


01:05:23.139 --> 01:05:26.475
But we keep trying.


01:05:31.814 --> 01:05:34.149
I'll tell you what I believe:


01:05:34.316 --> 01:05:36.234
If I am a rabbi,


01:05:36.401 --> 01:05:38.571
Jehovah is my God;


01:05:38.738 --> 01:05:41.698
If a mullah...
Allah the Merciful is He;


01:05:41.865 --> 01:05:44.408
If a Christian...
Jesus is my Lord.


01:05:44.575 --> 01:05:46.578
Here in Tressock,


01:05:46.745 --> 01:05:49.455
I believe the old religion
of the Celts


01:05:49.622 --> 01:05:52.083
fits our needs at this time.


01:05:56.213 --> 01:05:59.466
Isn't that all you can ask
of a religion?


01:06:17.398 --> 01:06:19.361
In a few moments, my friends,


01:06:19.527 --> 01:06:21.946
I will introduce you,
those who have not already met him,


01:06:22.112 --> 01:06:24.406
to your Laddie.


01:06:24.573 --> 01:06:26.617
Here he is.


01:06:26.784 --> 01:06:29.662
This year we are
exceptionally fortunate


01:06:29.828 --> 01:06:32.121
to have selected someone
who is both handsome


01:06:32.288 --> 01:06:34.165
and an excellent horseman.


01:06:34.333 --> 01:06:36.334
He really is a good man,


01:06:36.501 --> 01:06:38.544
worthy to be your Laddie.


01:06:38.711 --> 01:06:42.632
People of Tressock,
all hail the Laddie!


01:06:45.302 --> 01:06:47.595
You know your way
out of the village.


01:06:47.762 --> 01:06:51.307
In three long minutes, we'll be
after you. Remember what I told you.


01:06:52.475 --> 01:06:54.936
Now go!


01:06:59.315 --> 01:07:01.650
Go, Laddie, go!


01:07:38.102 --> 01:07:40.439
Just lie nice and still, miss.


01:07:40.605 --> 01:07:42.523
This will not hurt.


01:07:42.690 --> 01:07:45.192
You'll wake nice and fresh
tomorrow.


01:08:32.113 --> 01:08:33.989
Hurry, hurry, hurry.


01:08:34.156 --> 01:08:36.409
She'll be making
for the village.


01:08:36.576 --> 01:08:38.078
Oh.


01:08:38.244 --> 01:08:40.412
- And what is that?
- Alum.


01:08:42.581 --> 01:08:45.584
That American bitch.


01:08:45.751 --> 01:08:46.835
Can you believe the laird


01:08:47.002 --> 01:08:49.004
could have chosen a woman
that wicked as queen?


01:08:49.171 --> 01:08:51.799
Be still, man, will you?
You big baby, you.


01:08:51.965 --> 01:08:54.259
She nearly severed
one of your googerlies.


01:08:54.425 --> 01:08:56.677
We've just got to stop the bleeding
and you'll be fine.


01:09:00.099 --> 01:09:02.267
She'll be making
for a telephone.


01:09:04.019 --> 01:09:05.895
She'll need money.


01:09:06.062 --> 01:09:08.857
She's got no money, Daisy.


01:09:19.200 --> 01:09:21.076
Oh, Mr. Beame,


01:09:21.243 --> 01:09:23.120
you'll not forget
she's the queen?


01:09:23.286 --> 01:09:25.498
You'll respect that, man?
Promise.


01:09:25.665 --> 01:09:27.542
Oh, aye.


01:09:27.708 --> 01:09:30.877
She'll be in mint condition
for her coronation.


01:09:31.044 --> 01:09:34.424
I promise you that.
The bitch!


01:09:34.590 --> 01:09:36.466
Oh.


01:09:36.633 --> 01:09:38.635
You'll forget you heard that.


01:10:04.828 --> 01:10:06.829
Hey!


01:10:13.419 --> 01:10:15.463
Open the door.


01:10:37.358 --> 01:10:39.861
Come on.


01:10:41.070 --> 01:10:43.238
Steve!


01:10:55.335 --> 01:10:58.795
You're the guy with the raven.
Isn't that right?


01:10:58.962 --> 01:11:02.300
O wicker tree, O wicker tree,
tell me, what do you see?


01:11:02.467 --> 01:11:05.219
I'm sorry, sir,
I just need to use your phone.


01:11:05.385 --> 01:11:09.139
I need the cops... police.
You do have police?


01:11:09.306 --> 01:11:12.060
O wickerish tree,
O wickerish tree,


01:11:12.227 --> 01:11:13.936
t-tell me, w-what can you see?


01:11:14.102 --> 01:11:15.479
Oh, for God's sake,
where's your phone?


01:11:15.646 --> 01:11:17.482
My wickerish tree,
tell me, what do you see?


01:11:17.649 --> 01:11:20.192
- ♪ Don't eat people ♪
- ♪ Oh, no, not again ♪


01:11:20.359 --> 01:11:22.903
- ♪ I won't eat people ♪
- ♪ All the day long ♪


01:11:23.070 --> 01:11:25.572
- ♪ Don't eat people ♪
- ♪ He keeps on repeating ♪


01:11:25.739 --> 01:11:27.741
- ♪ Eating people is wrong... ♪
- It says, "Press 3."


01:11:27.908 --> 01:11:31.285
Um... No. One?


01:11:32.745 --> 01:11:35.414
This is crazy, mister.
How do you do this?


01:11:35.581 --> 01:11:37.417
♪ Eating people is bad ♪


01:11:37.584 --> 01:11:40.253
♪ But people have always
eaten people... ♪


01:11:40.419 --> 01:11:43.090
- Bitch.


01:11:43.257 --> 01:11:46.926
What's this music you're playing,
you miserable wee prick?


01:11:47.093 --> 01:11:50.012
Put me down!


01:11:51.472 --> 01:11:53.474
Let me go!


01:11:58.688 --> 01:12:00.897
It's a trap, Steve.


01:12:01.064 --> 01:12:02.274
Follow me, quick.


01:12:02.440 --> 01:12:05.235
Sure. It's just a game, Lolly.


01:12:05.403 --> 01:12:07.989
No, it's not a game.


01:12:10.282 --> 01:12:13.034
Please don't go, Steve.


01:12:14.036 --> 01:12:15.704
Steve!


01:12:25.671 --> 01:12:27.673
Oh.


01:12:37.684 --> 01:12:39.644
Come on, come on.


01:12:51.988 --> 01:12:53.323
Morning, Mr. Beame.


01:12:53.489 --> 01:12:54.867
Morning, Mary.


01:12:55.034 --> 01:12:57.536
Yes, well,


01:12:57.703 --> 01:13:00.039
I think we have excelled ourselves
this year.


01:13:00.205 --> 01:13:04.001
Beth really inspired everybody.


01:13:04.168 --> 01:13:06.711
Such a lovely girl,


01:13:06.878 --> 01:13:09.380
and that beautiful voice...


01:13:09.547 --> 01:13:12.967
the perfect queen.


01:13:15.928 --> 01:13:19.098
I've always wanted to ask...
why the oil?


01:13:19.265 --> 01:13:21.267
It's not as if you're going to
cook her.


01:13:21.434 --> 01:13:24.729
No, it just makes the skin
more flexible.


01:13:24.896 --> 01:13:28.608
It's easier to peel. I could use
the analogy of a peach.


01:13:28.775 --> 01:13:30.652
That's quite enough, Mr. Beame.
We don't want to hear


01:13:30.818 --> 01:13:33.111
the gory details, do we, Mary?


01:13:34.781 --> 01:13:38.200
Oh, no.
She's still breathing.


01:13:38.367 --> 01:13:40.702
Oh, yes.
She's just sedated.


01:13:40.869 --> 01:13:43.413
Mr. Beame likes the queen
to be absolutely fresh


01:13:43.580 --> 01:13:45.749
when he starts to work on her.


01:13:50.211 --> 01:13:52.465
What are you looking for?


01:13:52.631 --> 01:13:55.717
It's just one of these eyes


01:13:55.884 --> 01:13:58.679
are not at all the right color.


01:13:58.845 --> 01:14:02.724
Where is my bowl of eyes?


01:14:02.890 --> 01:14:06.227
It was on the shelf over there,
I could swear.


01:14:06.394 --> 01:14:08.896
That Dougie...


01:14:09.063 --> 01:14:11.107
he forgot to give them back.


01:14:11.273 --> 01:14:13.566
Are you mad, woman?


01:14:13.733 --> 01:14:17.531
You lent the queen's eyes,


01:14:17.698 --> 01:14:19.990
which are absolutely sacred


01:14:20.157 --> 01:14:22.451
and irreplaceable,


01:14:22.619 --> 01:14:25.329
to that idiot Douglas McCrea?


01:14:25.496 --> 01:14:28.581
He'll be riding after the Laddie
just now.


01:14:28.748 --> 01:14:31.419
You'll have to wait
until after the feast.


01:14:31.585 --> 01:14:34.295
As I thought...
hazel green,


01:14:34.462 --> 01:14:36.756
a wonderful color.


01:15:15.419 --> 01:15:18.547
Sleep a good sleep, my lovely.


01:16:23.985 --> 01:16:26.987
Hey, what took you guys
so long?


01:16:27.154 --> 01:16:29.532
Hope you brought some food,
'cause I'm starving.


01:17:19.746 --> 01:17:21.624
Laddie,


01:17:21.791 --> 01:17:25.587
you are a prince
among men, a king.


01:17:25.753 --> 01:17:27.672
We all...


01:17:27.839 --> 01:17:30.884
all salute you.


01:17:31.926 --> 01:17:33.760
You will give your life


01:17:33.927 --> 01:17:36.514
so that a new generation
of our people


01:17:36.681 --> 01:17:38.599
will be born
blessing your name.


01:17:38.765 --> 01:17:41.810
Children will be called
after you.


01:17:41.977 --> 01:17:44.897
Hallowed be thy name.


01:18:09.754 --> 01:18:11.839
Oh.


01:18:12.006 --> 01:18:14.008
Oh, God.


01:18:16.426 --> 01:18:18.430
Where am I?


01:18:20.139 --> 01:18:24.143
And now we will sing the hymn


01:18:24.310 --> 01:18:27.647
that you and Beth taught us.


01:18:27.813 --> 01:18:29.815
♪ Would you be free ♪


01:18:29.981 --> 01:18:32.985
♪ From your burden of sin? ♪


01:18:33.152 --> 01:18:35.695
♪ There's power in the blood ♪


01:18:35.862 --> 01:18:38.531
♪ Power in the blood ♪


01:18:38.698 --> 01:18:41.660
♪ Would you o'er evil ♪


01:18:41.826 --> 01:18:44.413
♪ A victory win? ♪


01:18:44.580 --> 01:18:47.457
♪ There's power in the blood ♪


01:18:47.624 --> 01:18:50.669
♪ Of the Lamb ♪


01:18:50.835 --> 01:18:53.797
♪ There is power, power ♪


01:18:53.964 --> 01:18:55.923
♪ Wonder-working power ♪


01:18:56.090 --> 01:18:58.510
♪ In the blood ♪


01:18:58.677 --> 01:19:01.178
♪ Of the Lamb ♪


01:19:01.345 --> 01:19:03.764
♪ There is power, power ♪


01:19:03.931 --> 01:19:05.850
♪ Wonder-working power ♪


01:19:06.016 --> 01:19:08.852
♪ In the precious blood ♪


01:19:09.019 --> 01:19:12.189
♪ Of the Lamb. ♪


01:19:12.356 --> 01:19:14.317
O blessed sun,


01:19:14.484 --> 01:19:18.529
our ancestors feared
one terrible winter's day


01:19:18.696 --> 01:19:21.281
that you would set
in the western sky,


01:19:21.448 --> 01:19:24.660
plunging us
into perpetual night.


01:19:24.827 --> 01:19:28.705
And yet you shine
upon us still.


01:19:28.871 --> 01:19:31.625
O glorious sun,


01:19:31.791 --> 01:19:34.043
accept our sacrifice


01:19:34.210 --> 01:19:36.254
that we may be fruitful


01:19:36.421 --> 01:19:38.882
once again.


01:19:41.510 --> 01:19:43.386
We pray


01:19:43.553 --> 01:19:46.265
that we may once more
hear the sound


01:19:46.432 --> 01:19:50.768
of children's laughter
in our midst.


01:20:19.087 --> 01:20:21.882
Steve.


01:20:58.460 --> 01:21:00.419
♪ Come with me, be with me ♪


01:21:00.586 --> 01:21:02.463
♪ Play with me
and love with me ♪


01:21:02.630 --> 01:21:04.464
- ♪ Come with me, be with me... ♪
- Oh.


01:21:04.631 --> 01:21:06.759
♪ Play with me
and love with me ♪


01:21:06.926 --> 01:21:08.803
♪ Come with me, be with me ♪


01:21:08.969 --> 01:21:10.887
♪ Play with me
and love with me ♪


01:21:11.054 --> 01:21:12.931
- ♪ Oh, tell me it's all right... ♪


01:21:13.098 --> 01:21:15.350
- ♪ Stay with me tonight... ♪
Hello?


01:21:15.517 --> 01:21:18.478
Let me out!


01:21:22.314 --> 01:21:24.318
Help!


01:21:25.693 --> 01:21:28.404
Let me out!


01:21:39.666 --> 01:21:42.334
Oh, God.


01:22:27.712 --> 01:22:29.630
Where's Steve?


01:22:29.797 --> 01:22:33.300
I tried to save him.
I begged him to follow me.


01:22:34.885 --> 01:22:36.970
He's dead, Beth.


01:22:37.137 --> 01:22:39.514
You're lying.
Where's Sir Lachlan?


01:22:39.681 --> 01:22:42.224
The Laddie is...


01:22:42.391 --> 01:22:44.395
is a sacrament.


01:22:44.562 --> 01:22:47.272
He's the perfect sacrifice.


01:22:47.439 --> 01:22:49.316
Beth, you have to believe me.


01:22:49.482 --> 01:22:51.485
I tried to save him.


01:22:51.652 --> 01:22:53.570
He thought it was
just a silly game.


01:22:53.737 --> 01:22:55.071
They killed him?


01:22:56.907 --> 01:22:59.283
They killed Steve?


01:23:00.952 --> 01:23:02.329
It isn't possible.


01:23:02.494 --> 01:23:04.371
Don't go that way.


01:23:04.538 --> 01:23:06.790
Don't you know what
they're going to do to you?


01:23:06.957 --> 01:23:09.084
Get on this horse now
and we'll go.


01:23:09.251 --> 01:23:12.172
If Steve's really dead,
I'm certainly not gonna run away.


01:23:12.339 --> 01:23:15.967
The Lord has chosen me
for this, Lolly.


01:23:16.134 --> 01:23:19.011
He saved me from Beame
and He will protect me now.


01:23:19.178 --> 01:23:21.222
You're forgetting
you're the Queen of the May.


01:23:21.388 --> 01:23:22.931
You're next.


01:23:23.097 --> 01:23:25.267
That's right.
I am one Queen of the May


01:23:25.434 --> 01:23:27.770
that no one is ever
gonna forget.


01:23:47.957 --> 01:23:51.834
♪ Wicker is woman ♪


01:23:52.001 --> 01:23:56.714
♪ She is a tree ♪


01:23:56.881 --> 01:24:00.884
♪ Soft and most tender ♪


01:24:01.051 --> 01:24:04.764
♪ And free ♪


01:24:10.477 --> 01:24:13.356
♪ Wicker is man ♪


01:24:13.523 --> 01:24:19.027
♪ And hard wood is he ♪


01:24:19.194 --> 01:24:22.656
♪ Strong are the arms ♪


01:24:22.823 --> 01:24:27.451
♪ Of the wicker tree ♪


01:24:32.291 --> 01:24:36.378
♪ Insatiable tree ♪


01:24:36.545 --> 01:24:41.674
♪ Part he and she ♪


01:24:41.841 --> 01:24:44.302
♪ O wicker tree ♪


01:24:44.469 --> 01:24:49.682
♪ Wicker tree. ♪


01:24:52.350 --> 01:24:54.186
Paul.


01:24:54.353 --> 01:24:56.604
Paul, what is it?


01:24:56.771 --> 01:24:59.859
It's the queen.


01:25:08.868 --> 01:25:11.119
Where's Steve?


01:25:11.286 --> 01:25:13.163
Is he really dead?


01:25:13.330 --> 01:25:16.165
Steve won, dear queen.


01:25:16.332 --> 01:25:18.418
You really should be
very proud of him.


01:25:18.585 --> 01:25:21.545
He was the finest Laddie
we ever had.


01:25:21.712 --> 01:25:24.049
Had?


01:25:28.887 --> 01:25:30.722
Danny,


01:25:30.889 --> 01:25:33.099
is Steve really dead?


01:25:34.142 --> 01:25:36.894
Aye, he is, my queen.


01:25:37.061 --> 01:25:39.730
And no one will ever
find his body.


01:25:39.897 --> 01:25:42.066
It is all gone.


01:25:42.232 --> 01:25:44.109
But his soul,


01:25:44.276 --> 01:25:46.570
his new self...


01:25:46.737 --> 01:25:49.073
it is in a heaven
beyond our imagining.


01:25:49.239 --> 01:25:51.076
Remember the song?


01:25:51.242 --> 01:25:53.994
He shalt have a horse
of the gods' own breed.


01:25:54.161 --> 01:25:56.205
He shalt have hounds
that can outrun the wind.


01:25:56.372 --> 01:26:00.125
Up there, nothing will be
too good for our wonderful Laddie.


01:26:00.292 --> 01:26:03.252
Steve was chosen
for his innate goodness.


01:26:03.419 --> 01:26:06.924
He is our gift to the gods,
and they will love him forever


01:26:07.091 --> 01:26:11.260
and reward us with renewed life
here in Tressock.


01:26:11.427 --> 01:26:14.263
Now, ladies and gentlemen,


01:26:14.430 --> 01:26:16.265
- it is time to...
- Murderer!


01:26:23.648 --> 01:26:24.816
No.


01:27:00.433 --> 01:27:02.644
Don't you have a song for this?


01:27:02.811 --> 01:27:05.813
"Auld Lang Syne," Perhaps?


01:27:05.980 --> 01:27:09.149
What, you don't like that one?


01:27:09.315 --> 01:27:12.070
How about your "Laddie" song?


01:27:12.237 --> 01:27:14.572
I don't really know the words,


01:27:14.738 --> 01:27:17.116
so you'll have to help me.


01:27:17.283 --> 01:27:20.119
♪ He shalt have horses ♪


01:27:20.286 --> 01:27:23.330
♪ Of the fairy breed. ♪


01:27:23.497 --> 01:27:25.790
Oh, come on, Danny, sing.


01:27:25.958 --> 01:27:28.127
Your king is dead.


01:27:28.294 --> 01:27:30.837
Will you sing for your queen


01:27:31.004 --> 01:27:33.381
and for my Laddie?


01:27:36.009 --> 01:27:38.471
♪ Delightful is the land ♪


01:27:38.637 --> 01:27:41.055
♪ Beyond all dreams ♪


01:27:42.516 --> 01:27:45.685
♪ Fairer than aught ♪


01:27:45.852 --> 01:27:50.565
♪ Thine eyes have ever seen ♪


01:27:50.732 --> 01:27:53.651
♪ There all the year ♪


01:27:53.818 --> 01:27:59.491
♪ The fruit is on the tree ♪


01:27:59.657 --> 01:28:01.783
♪ And all the year ♪


01:28:01.950 --> 01:28:06.581
♪ The bloom is on the flower ♪


01:28:06.748 --> 01:28:11.210
♪ There with wild honey drip ♪


01:28:11.376 --> 01:28:15.256
♪ The forest trees ♪


01:28:15.423 --> 01:28:18.759
♪ Nor pain nor sickness knows ♪


01:28:18.926 --> 01:28:22.386
♪ The dweller there ♪


01:28:22.554 --> 01:28:25.390
♪ Death and decay ♪


01:28:25.557 --> 01:28:31.189
♪ Come near him
nevermore... ♪


01:29:25.282 --> 01:29:28.743
I told Laddie he should have
brought his shooters.


01:29:28.910 --> 01:29:30.870
What's the use of a cowboy
without his shooters?


01:29:31.037 --> 01:29:32.330
Shooters?


01:29:32.497 --> 01:29:34.748
Steve... where did you
see him?


01:29:34.915 --> 01:29:37.085
Last night.
He was at the inn.


01:29:37.252 --> 01:29:38.794
It's so unfair.


01:29:38.961 --> 01:29:42.131
I'm not supposed to leave the house
during the May Day celebrations,


01:29:42.298 --> 01:29:44.300
but my mom and dad
wanted to go to the feast.


01:29:44.466 --> 01:29:46.510
I have to wait till I'm a man
they keep saying.


01:29:46.677 --> 01:29:49.846
Sweetheart, where's the nearest
village to Tressock?


01:29:50.013 --> 01:29:52.058
Am I going
in the right direction?


01:29:52.225 --> 01:29:54.101
Lancart's over there.


01:29:54.268 --> 01:29:57.646
Beth, if you want to avoid the road,
it's best to follow me.


01:29:57.813 --> 01:30:00.983
Okay, let's go.
Come on.


01:30:10.366 --> 01:30:13.494
I just want to go home.


01:30:43.023 --> 01:30:45.651
It's just a little bit further.


01:31:05.544 --> 01:31:07.046
No. No.


01:31:07.213 --> 01:31:08.756
Stay still.


01:31:08.923 --> 01:31:10.841
God!


01:31:14.262 --> 01:31:17.556
Lolly, push, push.


01:31:17.723 --> 01:31:19.225
Push.


01:31:22.144 --> 01:31:24.772
We have a little cowboy.


01:31:24.939 --> 01:31:27.399
Find us a man
to give us another.


01:31:27.565 --> 01:31:30.695
- And another.
- And another.


01:32:04.978 --> 01:32:09.482
♪ I know where I'm going ♪


01:32:09.649 --> 01:32:14.445
♪ I know who goes with me ♪


01:32:14.611 --> 01:32:18.407
♪ I know who I love ♪


01:32:19.700 --> 01:32:24.078
♪ My dear knows who I'll marry ♪


01:32:24.245 --> 01:32:28.583
♪ I have stockings of silk ♪


01:32:28.750 --> 01:32:33.464
♪ Shoes of bright green leather ♪


01:32:33.630 --> 01:32:38.050
♪ Combs to buckle my hair ♪


01:32:38.217 --> 01:32:43.015
♪ And a ring for every finger ♪


01:32:44.098 --> 01:32:48.102
♪ Featherbeds are soft ♪


01:32:48.268 --> 01:32:52.190
♪ Painted rooms are bonny ♪


01:32:52.356 --> 01:32:57.153
♪ But I would give them all ♪


01:32:57.320 --> 01:32:59.197
♪ For my handsome ♪


01:32:59.363 --> 01:33:02.700
♪ Winsome Johnny ♪


01:33:02.867 --> 01:33:06.829
♪ Some say he is poor ♪


01:33:06.996 --> 01:33:12.501
♪ I say he is bonny ♪


01:33:12.667 --> 01:33:16.129
♪ Fairest of them all ♪


01:33:16.296 --> 01:33:18.590
♪ Is my handsome ♪


01:33:18.757 --> 01:33:20.800
♪ Winsome Johnny. ♪


01:33:27.265 --> 01:33:31.311
♪ Cry not for me ♪


01:33:31.478 --> 01:33:33.355
♪ With the voice ♪


01:33:33.522 --> 01:33:36.315
♪ Of the angels ♪


01:33:36.482 --> 01:33:40.277
♪ Think not on me ♪


01:33:40.444 --> 01:33:42.071
♪ Though I'm far ♪


01:33:42.238 --> 01:33:45.658
♪ From your mind ♪


01:33:45.825 --> 01:33:49.495
♪ Dream only of me ♪


01:33:49.662 --> 01:33:51.747
♪ When you lie ♪


01:33:51.914 --> 01:33:54.668
♪ When you're sleeping ♪


01:33:54.835 --> 01:33:58.921
♪ For I have not gone ♪


01:33:59.088 --> 01:34:03.676
♪ From time's passing frame ♪


01:34:03.843 --> 01:34:08.012
♪ Though the sun, it will rise ♪


01:34:08.179 --> 01:34:13.351
♪ Cast a shadow over me ♪


01:34:13.518 --> 01:34:17.857
♪ I still see the picture ♪


01:34:18.023 --> 01:34:22.777
♪ Through time's passing frame. ♪


01:34:36.999 --> 01:34:39.167
♪ Life is ♪


01:34:39.334 --> 01:34:43.005
♪ The journey we must make ♪


01:34:43.171 --> 01:34:45.758
♪ To lead us ♪


01:34:45.925 --> 01:34:49.595
♪ To peace ♪


01:34:49.761 --> 01:34:52.890
♪ Ours is ♪


01:34:53.056 --> 01:34:55.350
♪ The Kingdom ♪


01:34:55.517 --> 01:34:58.687
♪ And a new life ♪


01:34:58.854 --> 01:35:02.148
♪ Is born again ♪


01:35:02.315 --> 01:35:04.483
♪ Born again ♪


01:35:04.650 --> 01:35:07.361
♪ Love is ♪


01:35:07.528 --> 01:35:09.947
♪ The answer ♪


01:35:10.114 --> 01:35:15.704
♪ Follow me ♪


01:35:17.580 --> 01:35:22.251
♪ Join in our journey ♪


01:35:22.418 --> 01:35:24.754
♪ We must pledge with love ♪


01:35:24.921 --> 01:35:30.175
♪ And with faith ♪


01:35:30.342 --> 01:35:36.097
♪ Over the mountains ♪


01:35:36.264 --> 01:35:40.144
♪ Where the sun rises ♪


01:35:40.311 --> 01:35:45.106
♪ Follow me, follow me ♪


01:35:45.273 --> 01:35:48.069
♪ Love is ♪


01:35:48.234 --> 01:35:50.487
♪ The answer ♪


01:35:50.654 --> 01:35:55.992
♪ Follow me. ♪

